\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Benchmark results for Fock state generation in a system consisting of a cavity coupled to a transmon. (a) Runtime per iteration and (b) memory usage versus Hilbert space dimension $d$. The dimension is varied by increasing cavity dimension while fixing the transmon dimension to 6. (c) Memory usage as a function of the number of time steps for $d=240$. All plots are in log-log scale. Dashed lines are power-law fits. (Parameters: $\Delta /2\pi =3\,$GHz, $g/2\pi =0.1\, $GHz, $\alpha /2\pi =-0.225\ $GHz and constant controls $a_z/2\pi =a_x/2\pi =0.1\ $GHz.)}}{26}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
