\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces  Optimization procedure to obtain detuning-robust $\hat  {X}_\theta $ gates in transmons. Input includes pulse constraints, transmon parameters, and a set of $M$ pulse durations. The choice of duration should be shorter than decay time $T_1$ and longer than $1/\epsilon _\text  {max}$, where $\epsilon _\text  {max}$ is the maximum pulse amplitude. Closed-system GRAPE is performed for each duration to obtain the corresponding pulse profiles. Subsequently, an open-system solver evaluates the cost function $C_\text  {o}$ for pulses with varying durations, selecting the pulse that minimizes $C_\text  {o}$.}}{34}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:optflow}{{6}{34}{Optimization procedure to obtain detuning-robust $\hat {X}_\theta $ gates in transmons. Input includes pulse constraints, transmon parameters, and a set of $M$ pulse durations. The choice of duration should be shorter than decay time $T_1$ and longer than $1/\epsilon _\text {max}$, where $\epsilon _\text {max}$ is the maximum pulse amplitude. Closed-system GRAPE is performed for each duration to obtain the corresponding pulse profiles. Subsequently, an open-system solver evaluates the cost function $C_\text {o}$ for pulses with varying durations, selecting the pulse that minimizes $C_\text {o}$}{figure.6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:optflow@cref}{{[figure][6][]6}{[1][33][]34}}
