\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Scaling of $\mu $, the number of matrix-vector multiplications. (a)-(d) The scaling of $\mu $ with $\left |\left |A\right |\right |_1$ for Hamiltonians $H_j$, $j=1,2,3,4$, when considering several error tolerances $\tau $. (e)-(h) The scaling of $\mu $ with dimension $d$ when considering $\tau =10^{-8}$ for each $H_j$, respectively. In all figures, dots are sampling data and solid lines are fitting curves. The parameters setup of $H_1,\ H_2$ are the same as the ones given in the captions of Figs.\ \ref {fig:state_time}, \ref {fig:gate}. Parameters of $H_3$ and $H_4$ are as follows: for $H_3$, $E_{Ci}/2\pi =2.5$\ GHz, $E_{Ji}/2\pi =8.9$\ GHz, $E_{Li}/2\pi =0.5$\ GHz, $g/2\pi =0.1\ $GHz and $\phi =0.33$ ; for $H_4$, $a_x^{(\nu )}/2\pi =a_y^{(\nu )}/2\pi =0.5$\ GHz and $g/2\pi =0.1$\ GHz. }}{39}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
